        'NUMBER, DATE AND UNIT CONVENTIONS ARE ONE PER DOCUMENT: the decimal separator is a comma in every figure, formula and tolerance ("1,5 milyon", "0,0065 mm", "34,984 mm", "32,5 µm", "9,81"); the thousands separator is a period from five digits up ("13.000", "150.000") while a four-digit technical figure may stay unseparated ("2500 d/d"); currency follows the number ("1.500 TL"); time is 24-hour; a form or contract date is DD.MM.YYYY but a press or news date is long ("25 Ağustos 2026"). Per-minute units are Turkish - l/dk, g/dk, kg/dk - and rotational speed is "d/d", never "obr/min" or "rpm". A unit symbol after a number stays lower case ("350 bar"), an exponent is a real superscript ("10⁻²", never "10^-2"), a numeric span takes a plain hyphen ("6-10 kat"). Never put -lAr on a noun after a number or in a stat counter: "13.000 proje", "40 lokasyon", "500 şirket". Turkish has no gender and no definite article; use the accusative -(y)I only for definite objects.',
