        'CORRELATIVES (ister...ister, hem...hem, ne...ne, gerek...gerek) MUST CARRY THE PARTICLE ON EVERY BRANCH, WITH EVERY BRANCH IN THE SAME SHAPE AND THE SHARED VERB AFTER THE LAST ONE: "İster sıfırdan başlayalım ister mevcut teknolojilerden yola çıkalım, ...". Never pair a verb-bearing branch with a bare noun or postpositional phrase, and never mix "ister" with "veya" or "ya da". English "Starting with either X or Y" and "Whether it is X or Y" translate left-to-right into exactly the broken shape, so re-read the first branch after drafting.',
